  "sheet_from": "Data/Object4/*.OZJ and .OZT, from MuMain, decoded under an nr_ prefix. The prefix is load-bearing for the reason the ground's is: assets/textures is one flat pool for every world, and yellow_jewel.png was already taken by an item.",
  "sheet_materials": {
    "wood02": "lamplight",
    "flower2": "foliage",
    "flower7": "bark",
    "flower9": "lamplight",
    "flower03": "foliage",
    "flower3": "foliage",
    "flower02": "foliage"
  },
  "material_note": "wood02: olive with a pale squiggle through it, drawn additively on both models that wear it.\nflower2: green and gold leaf rosettes round a stem - the giant plants' own body, and the single commonest surface on the map.\nflower7: grey-brown bark. Named flower and is a tree.\nflower9: a golden orb.\nflower03: leaf blades, green and gold, cut out.\nflower3: one broad leaf with its midrib.\nflower02: golden grass tufts, cut out.",
  "cutout": [
    "flower03",
    "flower02"
  ],
  "cutout_from": "Each carries a real alpha channel, as decode_texture reports it. Declared rather than detected - three separate attempts to read a cut-out off the art have been wrong, and the client decides it in code.",
  "additive": [
    "wood02"
  ],
